.nh
.TH "SYMVAULT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Symaira Vault" "Symaira Vault Manual"

.SH NAME
symvault-device-approval-pair - Pair a phone as an approval device for agent credential requests


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsymvault device approval-pair [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate a QR code a phone can scan to become an approval device: a
device that can approve or deny agent write requests when approval mode is
"prompt". This is unrelated to 'symvault device pair', which pairs a
second computer for vault-content sync and re-encrypts every entry —
approval-pair only grants the ability to approve/deny agent requests and
never touches vault encryption or entry content.

.PP
Requires 'symvault serve' to already be running with TLS (the default),
since the phone pins its connection to the server's certificate
fingerprint rather than trusting a certificate authority.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for approval-pair

.PP
\fB--host\fP=""
	LAN address the phone should connect to (auto-detected when omitted)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	When to emit ANSI color: auto, always, never

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output format shorthand for --output json; overrides --output when both are specified

.PP
\fB--no-pipe-warning\fP[=false]
	suppress 'reading from non-TTY' warning when piping secrets

.PP
\fB--output\fP="text"
	Output format (text, json, yaml)

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	use a named vault profile

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB--theme\fP=""
	Color preset: default, highcontrast, colorblind (or SYMVAULT_THEME)

.PP
\fB--vault\fP="~/.symvault"
	path to the password vault


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  symvault device approval-pair
  symvault device approval-pair --host 192.168.1.42
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsymvault-device(1)\fP
